    "id": "ACT-GRAM",
    "revision": 8,
    "title": "Describe consequences and manner in clauses",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk5-state-complements-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Describe consequences and manner in clauses",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "A complement after the linking particle can be an action phrase or a clause with its own subject. It describes the resulting state or manner, rather than the object of the first verb. A fixed expression such as 不得了 may follow 得 as an extreme-degree state complement.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "他累得不想说话。",
                "pinyin": "tā lèi de bù xiǎng shuōhuà 。",
                "meaning": "He is so tired that he does not want to speak.",
                "audio": "600eedc98e64a583200fc2d852fa753131eaf704084711598f709c6cea722eca"
              },
              {
                "text": "他说得大家都笑了。",
                "pinyin": "tā shuō de dàjiā dōu xiào le 。",
                "meaning": "What he said made everyone laugh.",
                "audio": "57674ad741407ea8abb3072fa728743c6a3ad1dff4d1be2aff71f6d0c8485b2e"
              },
              {
                "text": "我忙得不得了。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ máng de bùdéliǎo 。",
                "meaning": "I am extremely busy.",
                "audio": "689caebd3738da3efe9e8b29287fc409012a02cac0c63e3d92a1ea9cd79f2477"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Words used in this pattern",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "得",
                "pinyin": "de",
                "meaning": "used after a verb to describe how it is done",
